    {
      "sha": "027e293e5798d5ec1418683fbffdddfb2e4124bb",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/027e293e5798d5ec1418683fbffdddfb2e4124bb",
      "message": "refactor: share strict blueprint and validator identities (#663)",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-19T16:30:09Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "4cb2f23366cc9151662a9584da97814ed30c9acb",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/4cb2f23366cc9151662a9584da97814ed30c9acb",
      "message": "Return typed finalized deployment manifests from core\n\nMove the complete structural manifest type into core and return it from\nfinalized verification. Migrate node, fault-proofs, watcher, DA, and tooling\nconsumers while preserving verification rules and object ownership.\n\nAdd direct verifier rejection and ownership coverage. Correct the watcher\ntimeout expectation and synchronize the supervisor deadline test with actual\nrunner entry, retaining production timeout and deadline enforcement.\n\nValidation: workspace pnpm test (all lanes green), full DA suite, built core\nexports, changed-file ESLint/Prettier, and standards/spec reviews.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-17T22:33:59Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "348477771472da6550e652a8462be4de1da6d4b7",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/348477771472da6550e652a8462be4de1da6d4b7",
      "message": "Complete shared assembly migration for remaining cursor families",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-17T19:38:44Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "a4e78bc9ef3062ffa34cc9bfd34fe5085feb695f",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/a4e78bc9ef3062ffa34cc9bfd34fe5085feb695f",
      "message": "Fix funding-wallet authority in emulator reference publication",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-17T19:38:14Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "7fbd02d7fd6aa06ab4f97917c0b76460c14ebc3b",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/7fbd02d7fd6aa06ab4f97917c0b76460c14ebc3b",
      "message": "Derive workflow runner factories from total linear family definitions\n\nRemove crossBlockDuplicateEvent from the linear spec because its production\nworkflow uses the cursor adapter. Require a definition for every linear\ncategory and delete the temporary migration allow-list.\n\nDerive all 18 linear runner factories from the definitions table, retaining\nmodule-private admission and the dedicated DA hash preimage launch route.\nRemove the repeated exported constructors and update registration source\npaths without changing statuses or reasons. Watcher imports those removed\nconstructors, so switch its call sites to the corresponding factory rows.\n\nValidation (Node 22.23.1, pnpm 9.15.4):\n- Rebuilt gitignored plutus.json with aiken v1.1.23+5adf783 build --env testnet\n  before checks; 1149 entries, cross-block parameter lists match source.\n- Typecheck: fault-proofs, watcher, node, node-tools.\n- Lint: fault-proofs and the changed watcher file; changed-file formatting.\n- Vitest: manifest-bound-family-assembly, workflow, workflow-runtime,\n  linear-family-state, cursor-family-state, cursor-family-adapter,\n  da-hash-preimage: 7 files / 520 tests passed.\n- Additional cross-block-installed-lifecycle and\n  submit-init-emulator-da-hash-preimage: 8 failures. All 8 also fail on the\n  pre-change a1cc6a5de checkout with the freshly rebuilt blueprint; the\n  underlying error is Invalid native script witness. A fresh blueprint\n  alone does not resolve this emulator baseline failure in this environment.\n- Admission loop and public generic-constructor rejection unchanged.\n\nRefs #659, #657",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-17T17:07:04Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "a1cc6a5de27830e7fee8cc2bcc0afe8e70f497e2",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/a1cc6a5de27830e7fee8cc2bcc0afe8e70f497e2",
      "message": "Migrate the remaining linear families to the family assembly\n\nCommitted-field-shape, da-hash-preimage, double-withdraw, l2-tx-mistag,\nwithdrawn-reference-input and native-inclusion-two-step each declare a\nfamily definition and reduce their constructor to the manifest-bound\nassembly. Native-inclusion-two-step yields the invalidRange and zeroInput\ndefinitions over one shared transaction port; both keep their constructor\nnames.\n\nThe linear definitions table now holds eighteen of the nineteen linear\ncategories. The allow-list shrinks to crossBlockDuplicateEvent, whose spec\nrow is linear but whose live workflow runs on the cursor adapter; moving it\nonto the cursor arm or out of the linear spec is a separate decision.\n\nThe table test's certificate case now checks what the flag controls: the\ncertificate mint reference binding and the manifest refusal. Two of the\nmigrated ports read the certificate policy id into a step verdict without\nbinding the minting script, exactly as before the migration.",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-17T15:00:18Z"
    },
    {
      "sha": "a089207c8b0c87f7d3aade3efa4c263e18799621",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/Anastasia-Labs/midgard/commit/a089207c8b0c87f7d3aade3efa4c263e18799621",
      "message": "Assemble the receive-purpose-language cursor family from a family definition\n\nGeneralise the family definition so one definition type serves both adapter\narms: the linear arm keeps taking its step contract names and chain shape\nfrom the linear family spec, while the cursor arm carries the cursor spec,\nits step contract names, the optional action refiner and the cursor\ntransaction port. A fourth StepCount parameter, inferred from the cursor\nspec's literal step count, sizes the cursor arm's step tuples the way the\nlinear spec's tuple sizes a linear arm's. Every Linear* name stays as an\nalias over the family-wide type with the same parameters.\n\nThe assembly builds the cursor adapter from that arm with\ncreateCursorFamilyWorkflowAdapter instead of throwing, and checks that a\ncursor arm's spec agrees with its category and step contract names.\n\nMove receive-purpose-language onto the assembly: the family's constructor\nbecomes a check of its callback-free config and decision digest followed by\nthe assembly, `extend` supplies the actuator, lucid instance and state-queue\nlease coordinator the family's runner needs, and the constructor attaches\nthe invocation-bound decision digest. A sibling CURSOR_FAMILY_DEFINITIONS\ntable and a combined FAMILY_DEFINITIONS table sit beside the untouched linear\ntable, and the table-driven assembly test now covers both arms generically.\n\nRefs #658",
      "authorName": "Philip DiSarro",
      "authorDate": "2026-09-17T03:17:08Z"
    }
  ],
